description:
FILED s520a (Opus 5.5, 2026-10-18) while probing #3413's filename builtins with a handle.  SILENT WRONG (pre-existing: the fca3593b base answers the same).

REPRODUCER (perl 5.40.3):
    my $d = "/tmp/u-$$"; mkdir $d; open my $fh, '>', "$d/a" or die;
    print utime(10, 20, $fh), " ", (stat "$d/a")[9], "\n";
perl: `1 20` (utime on a FILEHANDLE is futimes(2) on its descriptor).  PCL: `0 <now>` -- p-utime passes every LIST element to utime(2) as a PATH, so the handle stringifies to a nonexistent name and nothing is touched.
FIX DIRECTION: p-utime's loop takes a handle-shaped element (the p-chmod / p-chown `streamp` arm) through futimes on the fd; sb-posix has no futimes (MEMORY: "stat-blksize/blocks/futimes ABSENT"), so it is an sb-alien call to futimens / futimes, or utimensat with the fd.  A platform-touching change: the install matrix + the macOS leg.
